I think here is possible to have an actionMap with using of event delegation

```
const actionMap = {
    "select-all": () => selectAllItems(),
    "select-none": () => selectNoneItems(),
    "select-custom": () => selectOnlyCustom(),
    "reset-selection": () => resetImportSelection(),
    "preview-selected": () => handleSelectiveImport(true),
    "import-selected": () => handleSelectiveImport(false),
};

previewContainer.addEventListener("click", (e) => {
    const actionEl = e.target.closest("[data-action]");
    if (!actionEl) return;

    const action = actionEl.dataset.action;
    actionMap[action]?.();
});
```

and the change event will be handle separately 

```
previewContainer.addEventListener("change", (e) => {
    if (e.target.matches('[data-action="update-count"]')) {
        updateSelectionCount();
    }
});
```
